<!-- Why 7 Years -->
<section class="section-pad bg-bg">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:72px;align-items:start;">
      <div>
        <div class="section-eyebrow">Why 7 Years?</div>
        <h2 class="section-title">The industry does one year. <em>We do seven.</em></h2>
        <p class="section-body">The standard 1-year contractor warranty is an industry minimum — it barely covers the time it takes for workmanship issues to surface. Most failures in a renovation happen in years two through five, when grout cracks, tile lifts, cabinetry shifts, or waterproofing fails. A 1-year warranty doesn't cover any of that.</p>
        <p class="section-body" style="margin-top:16px;">We offer 7 years because we know the failures won't come. We've been building in Massachusetts since 2001, and we build to last — not to the minimum. The 7-Year Warranty isn't a marketing claim. It's the economic outcome of building correctly the first time.</p>
        <p class="section-body" style="margin-top:16px;">Jesse DeBenedictis has four NARI certifications, including CKBR and CRPM — the most rigorous credentials in the remodeling industry. Those certifications require peer review of completed projects. You don't get them and then build sloppy work.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div style="background:var(--forge-950);border-radius:var(--r-2xl);padding:48px;color:white;">
          <div style="font-size:72px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:800;color:var(--ember-500);line-height:1;margin-bottom:16px;">7</div>
          <div style="font-size:28px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;color:white;margin-bottom:24px;">Years of Coverage</div>
          <div style="display:grid;gap:16px;">
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:start;"><div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ember-500);margin-top:7px;flex-shrink:0;"></div><div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--forge-300);line-height:1.6;">7× the 1-year industry standard</div></div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:start;"><div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ember-500);margin-top:7px;flex-shrink:0;"></div><div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--forge-300);line-height:1.6;">Covers all WORKS-provided labor and installation</div></div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:start;"><div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ember-500);margin-top:7px;flex-shrink:0;"></div><div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--forge-300);line-height:1.6;">Written, documented at project close</div></div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:start;"><div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ember-500);margin-top:7px;flex-shrink:0;"></div><div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--forge-300);line-height:1.6;">Single point of contact for all warranty claims</div></div>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:start;"><div style="width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ember-500);margin-top:7px;flex-shrink:0;"></div><div style="font-size:14px;color:var(--forge-300);line-height:1.6;">Product manufacturer warranties registered and managed by WORKS</div></div>
          </div>
